            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0606" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-15T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                                1924—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Department’s 27, March 11, 5 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d446-f1"/> The
                    Nicaraguan Minister for Foreign Affairs states that his Government is willing to
                    enter into a <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> through an exchange of
                    notes mutually according unconditional most-favored-nation treatment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
